+Sliced querysets can be used to limit the number of related objects prefetched
+per instance, using ``to_attr`` to store the result::
+
+    >>> restaurants = Restaurant.objects.prefetch_related(
+    ...     Prefetch('pizzas', queryset=Pizza.objects.order_by('name')[:3], to_attr='top_pizzas'))
+
+.. versionchanged:: 4.2
+
+    Support for prefetching from sliced querysets was added. It requires a
+    database backend that supports window functions.
+
 Custom prefetching also works with single related relations like
 forward ``ForeignKey`` or ``OneToOneField``. Generally you'll want to use
